    "body": "S013 closes an all-graph extremizer-selection step in the universal critical ASH* programme: exact loss-preserving even concentration under open-neighborhood inclusion, including zero/singleton receivers with the precise small STACK exception. Choosing GLOBAL Q then degree-weight P places heavy piles at minimal open neighborhoods; both extremal maxima restrict exactly to that domain. The residual incomparable-neighborhood inequality remains OPEN separately for STACK and CLEAR.\n\nThe session also gives a conditional CLEAR component comparison and private-exit/all-root THREE restrictions, and refutes actual gap-one first-shadow, adjacent CLOSED-neighborhood and threshold/global-Q deletion-independence proof shortcuts. These are auxiliary failures, not ASH* counterexamples. Complete proofs, dependency/hostile audit, primary attribution/equivalence limits and a complete strictly FUTURE S014 handoff are included. No delegation or later-stage work.\n\nValidation: 18 unchanged inherited check-only replays; six prior-hashed campaigns with 12 distinct producer/checkers; all 12 final check-only replays; governance validation including 130 immutable S013 artifact hashes; git diff --check. Full masks cover 291,639 inputs. Historical evidence/cutoffs remain unchanged. Hosted checks will be recorded from actual jobs.\n\nIntegration pin before PR creation: authored head ccfbdd7194c6571b5b9cbd780941777494f03073, tree b9811bdbf667c9e93df9a5001ebf30a036adb73b, sole parent/base main 1e28259f6e35849723bbe5e5fd545630498d45a9. One authored session commit. Ordinary non-force two-parent merge only; no auto-merge. Universal Phase1 stays IN_PROGRESS, phases2-6 unchanged/deferred; no human/kernel or worldwide-priority assurance.\n",
